        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "776e7650-e339-597c-a788-16008c35949a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Dog breeds: Labrador Retriever, Tibetan Terrier, Mastador\n- Dogs: Spike, Araki Fabulous Willy\n- Films and events: Old Yeller, Crufts\n\nFacts:\n- The Labrador Retriever, also called the Labrador, is a retriever-gun dog breed.\n- Some old travelers' accounts referred to the Tibetan Terrier as Dokhi Apso or \"outdoor\" Apso, indicating a shaggy or bearded working dog that lives outdoors.\n- Spike was a lop-eared yellow Mastador, a Mastiff and Labrador Retriever mix, and he was a dog actor best known for playing Old Yeller in Disney's 1957 film Old Yeller alongside Tommy Kirk, Dorothy McGuire, Fess Parker, and Kevin Corcoran.\n- Araki Fabulous Willy, also known as Willy, was a male Tibetan Terrier born on 25 April 2001 and died on 4 December 2008.\n- Araki Fabulous Willy won the Best in Show title at Crufts in 2007.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "1cc66ed5-56ee-5141-932a-d4b1f4762205",
        "text": "Page: Labrador Retriever. Sentence: The Labrador Retriever, also Labrador, is a type of retriever-gun dog.\nPage: Tibetan Terrier. Sentence: Some old travelers' accounts refer to the dog as Dokhi Apso or \"outdoor\" Apso, indicating a shaggy or bearded working dog which lives outdoors.\nPage: Spike (dog). Sentence: Spike was a lop-eared yellow Mastador (Mastiff/ Labrador Retriever mix) and a dog actor best known for his performance as Old Yeller in the 1957 Disney film of the same name co-starring Tommy Kirk, Dorothy McGuire, Fess Parker, and Kevin Corcoran.\nPage: Araki Fabulous Willy. Sentence: Araki Fabulous Willy (25 April 2001 – 4 December 2008), also known as Willy, was a male Tibetan Terrier who won the title of Best In Show at Crufts in 2007.",
